# *** THIS IS A PIPELINE SAMPLE, NOT A REVIEWED TRANSLATION. ***
#
# It exists to prove three things end to end and nothing else:
#   1. that `just po-extract` -> `just po-compile` -> the running shell works;
#   2. that a language with **six** plural forms survives the round trip
#      (Welsh is the reason ADR-0012 uses ngettext everywhere rather than
#      `if count == 1`); and
#   3. that a partly-translated catalogue degrades to en_GB per string rather
#      than per file.
#
# The ~20 strings below are ordinary, well-known words. Everything else is
# deliberately left untranslated. Before this ships to a family it needs a
# Welsh speaker, ideally one who teaches five-year-olds: docs/research/06 §4.7
# records the fall of 6.0 percentage points in Welsh among 5-15 year olds,
# which is why a Welsh kidnix is worth doing properly and not approximately.
#
